Assembler Version 20
====================
Assembled by: version 19 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 19, plus conditional assembly and variable
argument count:

Syntax:
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax (LDA, STA, etc.)
- All addressing modes (immediate, zero page, absolute, indexed, indirect)
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- .data directive for byte/string data
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Character literals: 'x', '\n', '\\', '\''
- Expression evaluation with + and - operators (left-to-right)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- Local labels with . prefix
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly with forward reference tracking
- Automatic zero page vs absolute addressing

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file
- .zeropage - switch to zero page section
- .code - switch to code section
- .data - declare raw byte data
- .ifdef label - begin conditional block if label is defined
- .endif - end conditional block

Command line:
- Variable argument count (2 or more arguments)
- define:label - pre-define a label with value $0001

Error handling: same as version 19, plus:
- err_endif_without_ifdef ($17): .endif without matching .ifdef
- err_unclosed_ifdef ($18): missing .endif at end of file
- err_label_expected ($19): .ifdef without label name
- err_invalid_arg ($10): replaces err_invalid_debug_arg with generic message

New in this version (relative to version 19):
- Conditional assembly with .ifdef/.endif
  - COND_DEPTH tracks nesting depth
  - SKIP_DEPTH records depth where skipping started
  - When skipping, only .ifdef and .endif are processed (for nesting)
  - Skip mode: lines parsed minimally to find directive keywords
  - skip_token function added for efficient skipping in conditional blocks
  - process_conditional_directive function dispatches ifdef/endif
- Command line define:label support
  - check_define_prefix parses "define:" prefix
  - Defined labels added to hash table with value $0001
  - Variable argument count via argc/argv (ARG_COUNT, ARG_INDEX)
  - Supports multiple define: arguments
- Error code $10 changed from "Invalid third argument" to generic
  "Invalid argument"

